  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">"Conglomeration is the gathering/collecting of elementary things; in other works, it is a return to elementary things. The Book, as an archival activity, is a referential process of elemental (basic) elements, of non-form, of what form is just beginning from (a reference to where the differences begin). But this is an artificial referring/massing; conglomerating of the pure and impure; together collecting ..." -- Artist's statement.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Images of letters of the Persian alphabet printed on heavy white paper interspersed with black and clear plastic sheets. Covers are black plastic over boards; bound with black string. Enclosed in 3-sided metal case; accompanied by portfolio containing certificate of authenticity, artist's statement and instructions for handling.</subfield>
  </datafield>
